According to the decision of the attestation commission, the attestation certificate is issued of specialists engaged in construction activities, the badge and stamp (where appropriate).

The following are recognized as certified specialists for the pursuit of the activities referred to in art. 339 para. (1) of the Town Planning and Building Code, persons holding certificates issued by the authorized institutions of the Member States of the Union European Union, unless the legislation of the Republic of Moldova establishes special mandatory conditions.

Specialists must meet the following general conditions:
•	have a university degree corresponding to the field(s) required for attestation;
•	be familiar with building legislation and regulatory documents;
•	be familiar with the provisions of the legislation and normative documents on quality in construction related to the execution of works.

Experience Requirements for project designers and bills of quantities developmers:
•	have at least 5 years of design activity in the required field for the attestation, including if the design is in the field of teaching, at least 3 years if they also hold a master's or doctorate degree in this field and at least 3 years for draftsmen;

Experience requirements for project reviewers and technical experts:

•	have at least 7 years in the field applied for attestation, practicing at the time of application for attestation for certification, and in the case of master and doctoral studies - a design activity of at least 5 years and/or hold a scientific-educational qualification; 
•	have a bachelor's degree corresponding to the field (field(s) applied for attestation or equivalent, confirmed by the central specialized education body;
•	have knowledge of building legislation and normative documents; have experience of implementation/supervision of authoring projects for construction projects in the Republic of Moldova.

Experience requirements for construction managers and project supervisors: 

•	have a higher education degree, in the case of construction manager, or a post-secondary technical vocational qualification in the case of project supervisors, corresponding to the field(s) applied for or another field equivalent, confirmed by the central specialized body in the field education;
•	have at least 5 years of executive activity after graduation from the institution higher education, in the case of site managers, and in the case of technical for technical - have at least 4 years of professional activity after graduation from a technical vocational education establishment or after 2 years after graduation from a higher education institution in the field applied for attestation;
•	knowledge of the provisions of the legislation of the Republic of Moldova and of the normative documents on quality in construction and execution of works.

Experience requirements for construction managers and project supervisors responsible for specialized works and building installations

•	have a university degree, in the case of project supervisors, or a post-secondary technical vocational degree, in the case of construction manager, corresponding to the field(s) applied for or equivalent, confirmed by the central specialized body in the field of education;
•	have at least 5 years of work experience after graduation from a higher education institution, in the case of project supervisor, and at least 4 years of work experience after graduation from a technical vocational education institution or 2 years after graduation from a higher education institution, in the field applied for attestation, in the case construction manager; 
•	be familiar with the provisions of the legislation of the Republic of Moldova and normative documents on quality in construction and execution of works

Experience requirements for specialist in construction testing laboratories:

•	possess a higher education degree or post-secondary professional technical qualifications corresponding to the requested field(s);
•	have laboratory experience of at least 5 years for Category I specialists, 3 years for Category II specialists, and 1 year for Category III specialists;
•	be knowledgeable in at least 6 testing profiles for Category I specialists, 3 testing profiles for Category II specialists, and 1 testing profile for Category III specialists;
•	be familiar with the provisions of the legislation and the normative documents concerning construction quality.


1.	The Applicant (or his legal representative) accesses the system (the Electronic Public Services Portal) either personally or with the assistance of the counter receptionist.
2.	The Applicant (or his legal representative) completes the application and uploads the necessary documents, either personally or with the assistance of the counter receptionist.
3.	If the Applicant (or their legal representative):
a) Submits the application and required documents with the assistance of the receptionist at the single-window counter, the receptionist shall:
•	Receive and duly register the application for technical-professional accreditation and accept the documents submitted by the applicant;
•	Immediately and unconditionally issue the applicant a confirmation certificate in accordance with the template indicated in Annex No. 3 to Law No. 160/2011; and
•	Forward the case (electronic copies of the application and submitted documents) to the issuing authority for review.
The application may be returned to the applicant only if it lacks the necessary information to identify the applicant or is missing required supporting documents.
b) submits the application and uploads the documents personally via the system, the system shall:
•	automatically generate an electronic confirmation document acknowledging receipt of the application and documents ("confirmation certificate"); and
•	automatically forward the application and supporting documents to the issuing authority.
4.	The issuing authority (the specialist) opens the case, examines the application and accompanying documents, and verifies compliance with legal requirements. If any documents or information expressly required by legislation are missing, the issuing authority (the specialist) shall suspend the examination period and immediately notify the applicant, specifying the grounds for suspension, the timeframe, and the remedial actions required to resume the examination process.
5.	The specialist reviews the case and conducts any necessary internal examinations before deciding on the issuance of the permitting document.
6.	The specialist either finalizes the permitting document or issues a rejection letter, providing legal justification based on the applicable provisions. The applicant shall be directly notified, and rejection shall occur only if the applicant fails to meet the conditions expressly stipulated by law or, where applicable, does not provide evidence of compliance within the suspension period. The decision shall be reviewed and signed by the director of the issuing authority.
7.	Once the permitting document (or rejection letter) is ready, the Applicant (or their legal representative) receives an electronic notification, downloads the permitting document, and confirms receipt.
8.	If the permitting document is issued in paper format (either upon request or as required by the issuing authority), the receptionist/specialist prints the permitting document, hands it over to the Applicant (or their legal representative), and confirms receipt.
